This project is licensed in two parts.


1. Source code: MIT License (full text in LICENSE-MIT)

   The general-purpose program logic in tower-study.html and assets/make_hero.py:
   rendering setup, camera and zoom controls, the interaction framework, the
   season, weather and time-of-day systems, the WebAudio synthesiser, the
   internationalisation mechanism, and the behaviour of the HUD; plus build.sh,
   _headers and the scripts in tools/.

   You may reuse these techniques in any project, commercial or not.


2. The artwork: PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0 (full text in LICENSE-POLYFORM-NC)

   The Tower Study as a creative work: the design, modelling and arrangement of
   the tower, its rooms, furniture, props and characters; its colours, procedural
   textures and visual style; the visual design of the HUD; the written copy in
   window.I18N; the melodies; the images in assets/ (hero.svg, divider.svg) and in
   static/ (og-image.png, favicon.svg, favicon.ico, apple-touch-icon.png),
   including the drawing data in assets/make_hero.py that produces them.

   You may use, change and share the artwork for any noncommercial purpose.
   Commercial use of the artwork needs a separate license from the copyright holder;
   contact SummerPapaya on GitHub.

   Where the two parts overlap, for example when code is copied in a way that
   reproduces or adapts the tower, its rooms or their look, the PolyForm
   Noncommercial License 1.0.0 applies.


3. Not covered by either license

   Third-party components are redistributed under their own licenses:
   three.js r160 in static/three-r160/ (MIT, see static/three-r160/LICENSE), and
   subsets of the fonts Cormorant Garamond, Noto Serif SC and ZCOOL XiaoWei in
   static/fonts/ (SIL Open Font License 1.1, see the OFL-*.txt files there).

   The moon floor lamp is a fan homage to the moon chair in Nintendo's Animal
   Crossing. This project is not affiliated with or endorsed by Nintendo.


